# compiler issue: checking an integer-backed enum is cubic in its number of cases.
#
# luce-base 0.23.0 on an M-series Mac: `luce-base check` of this file (800 cases) takes 6.3 s;
# 200 cases 0.10 s, 400 cases 0.79 s, 1600 cases 51 s (time x8 per doubling). A plain enum
# (no `as`) or a struct with 800 fields checks in 0.02 s. Ladybird's generated CSS enums have
# 850 (Keyword) and 409 (PropertyID) cases, so luce-browser-css's css_data module takes 8 s to
# check and every module that imports it pays that again.
#
# Expected: linear (or n log n) time, like the plain enum.

